{
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-8155a24e-7fff-c85c-1fd1-d95f6f1095e0&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;The proposed rear extension, by reason of its scale, form, and detailed design, would be an unsympathetic and visually intrusive form of development, failing to respect the character and appearance of the hosting dwelling and the wider terrace, where such proposals are an uncharacteristic feature. As such, the proposal is contrary to Policies D3 (Optimising site capacity through a design-led approach) of the London Plan (2021), LP1 (Design Quality and Local Character) of the Hackney Local Plan (LP33), and the Residential Extensions and Alterations SPD (2009).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
